Hello! This repo was made with the intent on how to show users on how to put a silent voice on their PSP 1000/2000/3000
There are TWO METHODS. One: Use a dvd version - Two: Use a digital version (assuming you have the mp4 ready to go)

# DISCLAIMER:
THIS REPOSITORY IS NOT WITH AN INTENT TO ALLOW USERS TO USE PIRATED
COPIES OF THE FILM. THIS REQUIRES A LEGALLY OBTAINED COPY OF THE MOVIE. THIS PROCESS MAY BE ILLEGAL WHERE YOU
LIVE EVEN WITH A LEGAL COPY, SO PLEASE DO YOUR RESEARCH.

## Method 1: DVD/BLUERAY COPY
Make sure you have two things ready: a functional dvd drive connected to your PC (requires windows), and a dvd copy of a silent voice

So first, download an app called MakeMKV from the releases page, and Handbrake alongside the PSP Preset file. (also in the releases)

First head into MakeMkv. Press the DVD icon: Wait for it to do its thing.

Once done, you will see a page Showing three checkboxes next to three text variables saying "TITLE"
Uncheck all except the top one with TWELVE "Chapters"
Then you may click the button underneath the text saying "Make MKV"

WARNING!!! ONCE YOU CLICK MAKE MKV IT WILL TAKE A LONG TIME TO CONVERT

## Method 1 & 2: DVD/BLUERAY/DIGITAL

Once that process is complete, take the finished MP4 copy, and head into After Burner. 
Highlight the Presets option in the top, and click "Import from file" use the PSP Preset file from earlier,
and then once done, select the "Add To Queue" Button, import the MP4, then press the Preset button under the Title Button,
select your PSP Preset. Now, hit the "Start Encode" Button. Wait around, once complete you should be ready to put
the newly converted copy in the video folder on your PSP Memory Stick!

### Note:
This Process may or not work with other films or show episodes from different series, 
I haven't Personally Tested it.
